{
  "id": "29259_itagaru",
  "headword": "{痛|いた}がる",
  "reading": "いたがる",
  "romaji": "itagaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to show signs of pain; to complain of pain",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to show signs of pain; to act as if in pain; to complain of pain",
      "explanation": "To outwardly express or behave as though feeling pain. Formed from the adjective {痛|いた}い plus the suffix ～がる, which describes another person's visible feelings rather than one's own."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29259_itagaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもが{足|あし}を{痛|いた}がる。",
      "english": "The child is complaining that their leg hurts.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29259_itagaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{注射|ちゅうしゃ}を{痛|いた}がって、{泣|な}き{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "Dreading the pain of the shot, the child started crying.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29259_itagaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{犬|いぬ}がしきりに{耳|みみ}を{痛|いた}がるので、{動物病院|どうぶつびょういん}に{連|つ}れて{行|い}った。",
      "english": "Since the dog kept showing signs that its ear hurt, I took it to the vet.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). The painful body part or cause is marked with を: {足|あし}を{痛|いた}がる, {注射|ちゅうしゃ}を{痛|いた}がる.\n\nUSAGE:\nThe ～がる suffix describes a third person's outward signs of feeling, so {痛|いた}がる is used about others, not oneself. To say your own leg hurts, use {足|あし}が{痛|いた}い, not {足|あし}を{痛|いた}がる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ひどく{痛|いた}がる: to be in evident severe pain\n- {患部|かんぶ}を{痛|いた}がる: to show pain in the affected area\n- {痛|いた}がって{泣|な}く: to cry from pain",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
